<p>Armed groups launched coordinated attacks across Mali on Saturday, including in Bamako, Kati, and cities in the center and north, in one of the country’s largest such assaults in recent years. Multiple reports said the al-Qaeda-linked Jama’at Nusrat al-Islam wal-Muslimin, or JNIM, claimed responsibility, while Reuters reported that SITE Intelligence Group said JNIM and the Tuareg-led Azawad Liberation Front, or FLA, jointly claimed full responsibility. Witnesses described explosions and gunfire near Bamako’s airport and around Kati, home to a major military base, as security forces responded and blocked roads. Mali’s army said it was fighting armed “terrorist groups” and later said the situation was under control, though operations were still continuing. The scale and geographic spread of the attacks pointed to a sharp escalation in Mali’s long-running conflict, which has involved jihadist groups, separatist movements, and a military-led government backed in recent years by Russian security support. The immediate picture remained fluid, with competing claims about battlefield gains and no independently verified nationwide casualty toll available across the cited reports.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vI-CC_d-fKePTXEmG1nbufk2pbgilL_s_gKty62rZWGtUkwFnD4QrnutqecG8qH4r-AZTU3dwFeu04F76JZg24cJar1xGITvodWGfrEov2BDuwA_TYE-aPlb8C6GRXCIs5nbmDkgB8SMryP7Xrpylahj0sLZu84wGFRJVcorYlLJZerpmQHLfLNlTlxFLOq10lbO2p5riz0d7waXELAlMBH8e1066mmhDUxTry-jvO7Kd-08qahuyhPzxkHzwKcNjQ_bdPPcQxZdw8rd8Q' alt='A Malian soldier stands in position during an attack on the Kati military base outside Bamako on Saturday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Cities targeted: Reports said strikes or fighting hit Bamako, Kati, Sévaré, Gao and Kidal, showing an unusually broad operational reach across southern, central and northern Mali.</li><li>Airport disruption: The U.S. Embassy in Bamako issued a security alert after explosions and gunfire near Kati and the international airport, telling U.S. citizens to shelter in place and avoid travel in the area.</li><li>Government claim: Army spokesperson Col. Souleymane Dembele said at least 80 militants were eliminated, while another report said the military claimed several hundred assailants had been killed; those figures had not been independently verified in the source set.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Malian army: The military said it was engaging armed groups, later declared the situation under control, and said follow-up operations were still underway. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/gunmen-attack-several-locations-across-malis-capital-11409484#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>JNIM and FLA: The armed groups described the attacks as a joint operation, with JNIM claiming strikes on military and airport targets and Reuters reporting that SITE said both groups claimed full responsibility. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/al-qaeda-linked-jnim-says-it-carried-out-mali-attacks-with-tuaregled-fla-site-2026-04-25/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>U.S. Embassy in Bamako: The embassy warned Americans to shelter in place and avoid travel near the affected areas around Kati and the airport. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/islamic-militants-separatists-claim-simultaneous-attacks-across-mali/article70906721.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Financial Times analysis: The paper described the attacks as a direct test of Mali’s Russian-backed military government and its ability to contain simultaneous assaults by jihadist and secessionist forces. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/fabb00f4-7997-49e2-a30b-41fb7caa6d59'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/clyx7nnrkqdo'>Explosions and gunfire as armed groups launch co-ordinated attacks across Mali</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/islamic-militants-separatists-claim-simultaneous-attacks-across-mali/article70906721.ece'>Islamic militants, separatists claim simultaneous attacks across Mali</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/25/world/africa/mali-attacks-jnim-al-qaeda-bamako.html'>Al Qaeda-Linked Militants Launch Major Attacks on Cities Across Mali</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/gunfire-blasts-rock-mali-attackers-hit-capital-cities-132372626'>Gunfire and blasts rock Mali as attackers hit capital and other cities, residents say</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/mali-army-bases-hit-in-large-scale-attacks-claimed-by-al-qaeda-linked-militants'>Mali army bases hit in large-scale attacks claimed by al-Qaida-linked militants</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/gunmen-attack-several-locations-across-malis-capital-11409484#publisher=newsstand'>Gunmen Attack Several Locations Across Mali&#x27;s Capital</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/fabb00f4-7997-49e2-a30b-41fb7caa6d59'>Co-ordinated attacks threaten Mali’s Russian-backed regime</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/africa/639069-mali-coordinated-terrorist-raids/'>Mali hit by wave of coordinated terrorist raids</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604250226.html'>Mali: Bamako and Other Locations Target of Coordinated Attacks</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/islamic-militants-and-separatists-attack-several-locations-in-malis-capital-and-other-cities'>Islamic militants and separatists attack several locations in Mali&#x27;s capital and other cities</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/25/militants-and-separatists-launch-coordinated-attacks-across-mali'>Militants and separatists launch coordinated attacks across Mali</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-mali-hit-by-large-scale-attacks-claimed-by-al-qaeda-linked-militants/'>Ma